meta {
  name: 29 EMI - Submit Result (both analytes)
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

get {
  url: {{emiBaseUrl}}/emi/submitResult
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  TOKEN: {{flowAdapterToken}}
  Content-Type: text/plain
}

body:text {
  {
    "specimen_type": "",
    "tube_information_id": "e9b6927a-f2e0-4898-910b-d892b45d8de1",
    "equipment_id": "11111112",
    "tube_no": "{{sampleBarcode}}",
    "original_tube_no": "{{sampleBarcode}}",
    "result_date": "1668583670356",
    "sent": "",
    "sent_date": "",
    "status": "-1",
    "local_db_status": "1",
    "test_results": [
      {
        "test_result_id": "b0a69d67-4434-44f0-b1e5-cf43f83bc536",
        "test_result": "{{emiResultValueA}}",
        "test_name": "{{emiParamNameA}}",
        "display_name": "{{emiParamNameA}}",
        "universal_test_id": "{{emiParamCodeA}}",
        "unit": "{{emiParamUnitA}}",
        "result_type": "",
        "specimen_types": []
      },
      {
        "test_result_id": "c1b70e78-5545-55a1-c2f6-df54e94cd647",
        "test_result": "{{emiResultValueB}}",
        "test_name": "{{emiParamNameB}}",
        "display_name": "{{emiParamNameB}}",
        "universal_test_id": "{{emiParamCodeB}}",
        "unit": "{{emiParamUnitB}}",
        "result_type": "",
        "specimen_types": []
      }
    ],
    "comment": "auto from analyzer (EMI Panel E2E)",
    "token_id": "{{flowAdapterToken}}",
    "adapter_id": "14",
    "adapter_code": "erba-h560"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const b = res.body;
  if (b && b.report_log && b.report_log.log && b.report_log.log.length) {
    const filled = b.report_log.log.filter((l) => l.fill_status === "Report filled");
    bru.setVar("emiFilledCount", String(filled.length));
  }
}

tests {
  test("result accepted (legacy s=200)", function () {
    expect(res.body.s).to.equal("200");
  });
  test("PANEL: BOTH member reports filled from one submit", function () {
    expect(res.body.m).to.equal("Result updated successfully");
    expect(res.body.test_status).to.match(/2 test updated/);
    const filled = res.body.report_log.log.filter((l) => l.fill_status === "Report filled");
    expect(filled.length, "reports filled").to.equal(2);
  });
}

docs {
  **Machine step 2 — submit BOTH analyte results.** A **GET** to `/emi/submitResult`
  with a JSON body under `Content-Type: text/plain` (legacy quirk); auth is the
  **`TOKEN`** header. `tube_no` is the shared panel **`sampleBarcode`** — the same
  specimen id the analyzer received in step 28.
  
  `test_results[]` carries **two** entries, one per member: `universal_test_id`
  `{{emiParamCodeA}}` / `{{emiParamCodeB}}` match the parameter codes on the two
  member tests, so each value fills its member report. Both member reports are
  fillable (PENDING, from step 25) and adapter-mapped, so both are written with
  **`source = ADAPTER`** and moved to **`SAVED`** → `test_status: "2 test updated"`
  with two `fill_status: "Report filled"` log lines. Captures `emiFilledCount`.
}
